    63	### P8F-01 — PROOF-GAP: Lemma 9 infers equal hashes from signature verification
    64	
    65	**Exact location:** `PROOF.md:320–328`, especially 325: “If … differs … a hash
    66	match is a collision.” Verification by the same ECDSA packet does not establish
    67	that hash match. This also limits the signature-reuse implication in Remark 10
    68	(`PROOF.md:339–341`); different message bytes alone do not prove signature
    69	separation under only assumption H.
    70	
    71	There is an actual SHA-256/OpenPGP witness, not merely a hypothetical pair of
    72	digest values. Two different codec-accepted attestation frames have different
    73	SHA-256 digests of `F || T` with the same first 16 bits. One rule-O packet verifies
    74	over both under one chosen P-256 public key, including I's signature policy.
    75	
    76	Reproduce:
    77	
    78	```sh
    79	prototype/.venv/bin/python -B prototype/p8-falsify/targeted.py lemma9
    80	```
    81	
    82	Output:
    83	
    84	```text
    85	lemma9 actual-frame witness: attempts=195 indices=(114, 194)
    86	frames-distinct=True SHA256-digests-distinct=True left16-equal=True
    87	same-key same-packet B-verifies=[True, True] I/OpenSSL-verifies=[True, True] sig-policy=OK
    88	F0/F1 codec B=OK/OK I=OK/OK
    89	digest0=67c0a82553460d29163acd32374032434e0ec725c4be64909da5e7b784b88f4d
    90	digest1=67c0c2f2e0361ca224f296d2a5cadec3808453a94b47325d555d0e20b30b5d3d
    91	The chosen key does not match the frames' illustrative key_fp; no complete receipt is claimed.
    92	```
    93	
    94	Construction: let `r = x(2G) mod n`, let `z0,z1` be the actual digest integers,
    95	choose `d = -(z0+z1)/(2r) mod n`, and set `s = (z0+rd)/2 mod n`.
